00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.550 align:start position:0%
 
what's up ladies and gentlemen welcome  back for another a song of ice and fire  video  well folks once again george rr martin  has missed another deadline that he set  upon himself  the internet was absolutely on fire  yesterday as hundreds or even  thousands of fans were making fun of  george rr martin because another  deadline has come and gone without any  announcements of him having the winds of  winner done  and in hand now just in case you're  wondering what i am referring to  let me back up a little bit this all  started because of something george r  martin said  on his not a blog back in may of last  year  this is what he said in the summer of  2020 wellington is hosting the world  science fiction convention  the oldest and most important con in the  science fiction  fantasy calendar and they've asked me to  serve as toastmaster for the hugo awards  writers fans and artists from all over  the world will be headed down to check  out all of your wonders  i hope lots of you kiwis will join us of  course  i was especially moved by your offer to  bring me to new zealand on  us how wonderfully generous as it  happens  i do have enough money to make it to new  zealand on my own  but there are many american writers fans  and artists who do not  if you'd care to fly say 20 or 30 or 50  of them to wellington in place of me  i have no doubt they would instantly  accept and fall in love with middle  earth  or new zealand just as i have and you  have such big planes  i'm sure you could squeeze them in as  for finishing my book  i fear that new zealand would distract  me entirely too much  best leave me here in westeros for the  nonce but i tell you this  if i don't have the winds of winter in  hand when i arrive in new zealand for  worldcon  you have here my formal written  permission to imprison me  in a small cabin on white island  overlooking that lake of sulfuric acid  until i'm done just so long as the acid  fumes do not screw up my old dos word  processor  i'll be fine so as you can see over a  year ago  george r martin said he would have the  winds of winner finished by the summer  well it's now the summer of 2020 and  george has yet to deliver the next book  in fact it sounds like he's not even  close to having it finished  he gave us another wins of winner update  very recently and this is what he said  i have to confess after half a year of  pandemic  quarantine and social distancing i am  showing signs of cabin fever  half of a witch is quite literal in my  case yes  i am in an actual cabin in the mountains  no i have no fever  yay for the present at least i am  healthy  for an out-of-shape guy at 71 at least  and doing all that i can to stay that  way if nothing else  the enforced isolation has helped me  right i am spending  long hours every day on the winds of  winter and making steady progress  i finished a new chapter yesterday  another one three days ago and another  one the previous week  but no this does not mean that the book  will be finished tomorrow or published  next week  it's going to be a huge book and i still  have a long way to go  i was heartbroken when khan zealand was  forced to go  virtual due to the pandemic and i have  to cancel my plans  exciting plans for a long trip down to  wellington with paris and my minions  but there is definitely a silver lining  in that cloud  the last thing i need right now is a  long interruption that might cost me  all my momentum i have built up i can  always visit wellington next year  when i hope that both covet 19 and the  winds of winner will be done  i still plan to host the hugo awards and  fulfill all the rest of my toastmasterly  duties for worldcon  and have started pre-recording some bits  for the ceremony  a wise precaution since i am hopeless  with zoom  and skype and like things but that is a  lot less time consuming  and distracting than flying to the other  end of the world  in between tapings i returned to  westeros  of late i have been visiting with cersei  osha  tyrion sir barristan and area hota  i will be dropping back into bravo's  next week i have bad days which get me  down  in good days which lift me up but all in  all i am pleased with the way things are  doing  i do wish they would go faster of course  way way back in 1999  when i was deep in the writing of a  storm of swords i was averaging about  150 pages of manuscript a month  i fear i shall never recapture that pace  again  looking back i am not sure how i did it  then a fever indeed  well george r martin should be in new  zealand as we speak  with the winds of winter in his hand but  as you can see  he is not in new zealand and the book is  far from finished  this is something we have seen from him  over and over again  year after year now to be honest with  you i'm not even mad about him missing  another deadline  i never expected him to actually have  the book done by this summer  what i don't understand is why he keeps  giving himself these deadlines when he  knows he'll never make them  he has even said that he is done  announcing deadlines because he has  missed every one  but for some reason he has done it here  again he says he still has a long way to  go  and he hopes he can have it done by next  summer when new zealand has another  convention  by then it will have been a decade since  the dance with dragons was released  all i can do now is hold out hope that  he will get it done sometime soon  whenever the winds of winter does come  out i expect it to break the internet  as well as breaking records for the  amount of sales a song of ice and fire  was already a very successful series of  books but after that disaster of a  finish we got from game of thrones  i think the anticipation for the winds  of winter is through the roof  however with that being said let's look  at another update from george rr martin  he said this just a little over a week  ago this writing stuff is hard  even so it has been going well of late  three more chapters completed this week  and good progress on several more  still a long long way to go though do  not get too excited  yikes no matter how long it actually  takes  i am very confident we will get the ones  of winter and it will most likely be one  of the greatest books of all time  but at this rate i am not so sure about  the dream of spring  for now it will have to remain a dream  for those of you that don't know i am  making videos on every chapter from  every book and a song of ice and fire  i have only recently started but it  looks like i will have enough time to  get them finished before the next book  is released  i think if you haven't had a chance to  read the books yet  head over to my most recent videos i am  making videos on each chapter  letting you know what happens in the  books starting from the very beginning  i would love to see you there anyways  let me know what you all think about  these different updates from george rr  martin  do you think he will ever finish a song  of ice and fire  leave your thoughts down below i would  love to see what you have to say  if you would like to support my channel  consider heading over to my patreon  i would really appreciate that either  way i hope everyone has a great day  i will see you again very soon with my  next chapter video  bye  [Music]  [Music]  um  you

